    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29023" root="عزى" body-key="E">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَزِىَ</span></b> , (Msb, K, and Ham p. 369,) aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَزَىَ</span></b> ,
(Msb,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَزَآءٌ</span>; (K;) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَزَى</span>, (Ham ubi
suprà,) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَزَا</span>, inf. n. as above; (Ham p. 125;)
<i>He was,</i> or <i>became, patient,</i> or <i>enduring,</i> (Msb,
K, and Ham,) or <i>commendably so,</i> (K,) <i>of that
which befell him.</i> (Msb.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَزَاهُ إِلَى أَبِيهِ</span>, first
pers. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَزَيْتُهُ</span>, aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَزِىَ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَزْىٌ</span>: see 1 in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عزو</span>.
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [Hence,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَزَيْتُ الحَدِيثَ</span>, aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَعْزِيهِ</span>, <i>I traced
up,</i> or <i>ascribed,</i> or <i>attributed, the tradition</i> [<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِلَى</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَائِلِهِ</span> <i>to the original relater thereof</i>]; syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَسْنَدْتُهُ</span>.
(Msb, TA. *)

